      "name": "My Stack Simulator, (Wed, Jul 8th)",
      "description": "The stack is a memory region where a program stores temporary data -&#;x26;#;xc2;&#;x26;#;xa0;like local variables and return addresses. This simple mechanism is what allows programs to call functions&#;x26;#;xc2;&#;x26;#;xa0;within functions, and always find their way back -&#;x26;#;xc2;&#;x26;#;xa0;but it&#;x26;#;39;s also precisely why a stack that grows too large, or gets overwritten with unexpected data, becomes a favorite target for attackers looking to hijack a program&#;x26;#;39;s execution flow.",
